  <!--
    Meridian MSR+ codes for the DSP5500, RC5X (extended RC5) at 36kHz.

    Supplied as raw microsecond timings and verified by decoding each one
    as RC5 Manchester: all 32 quantise onto the 889us half-bit grid, all
    yield a 14-bit frame with start bit 1 and address 19, and no two
    frames or commands collide. Address 19 is what the existing MSR.xml
    codes decode to as well.

    The <ccf> payloads below are re-encoded from the decoded frames using
    canonical RC5 timings (889us / 1778us) rather than transcribed, so
    they carry no capture jitter; each one was checked to decode back to
    the same 14 bits. Deviation from the supplied timings peaks at 21us.

    S2 is the RC5X field bit: 0 means the 6-bit command is extended by 64.
    Skip/Scan carry S2=1, i.e. they are plain RC5 commands 33/50/52.
  -->
